    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0915" n="829" xml:id="pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to the Presidents Special
                        Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d444-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Casablanca</hi></placeName>,] <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1943-01-24T23:59:59+01:00"
                            notBefore="1943-01-12T00:00:00+01:00">undated</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I suggest that U.S. Chiefs of Staff should be informed that shipments on ground
                    equipment and aircraft to the French should only be undertaken at a rate to be
                    determined by Combined Chiefs of Staff which will not prejudice military
                    operations agreed on at Casablanca.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d444-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d444-f1-content">
                <p>Attached to this document is the following note by Hopkins dated April 10, 1943:
                    “This is a memorandum Churchill handed me at Casablanca.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
